# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESTRICTED DATA — DO NOT REMOVE
#
# data/ holds two kinds of licensed content that must never be committed:
#   - MIMIC-IV note text, under the PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data Use
#     Agreement. Ship data/notes.sql (the extraction query) instead.
#   - The UMLS Metathesaurus, under the UMLS Metathesaurus License Agreement.
#
# This block is DEFAULT-DENY on purpose. An allowlist of extensions is one
# unanticipated file type away from leaking (a .zip, a .RRF, a differently
# cased directory), so everything under data/ is ignored and the few
# publishable files are re-admitted by name below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/.gitkeep

# Belt-and-braces: these must never be committed from anywhere in the tree,
# whatever they are called or wherever they are dropped.
*.RRF
*.rrf
*.zip
*.duckdb
**/[Uu][Mm][Ll][Ss]/
**/[Mm][Ee][Tt][Aa]/

# Derived artifacts that may embed restricted text
**/annotations.parquet
**/*.annotations.json
.robustehr_cache/
out/
runs/
release/text/

# Secrets
#
# API keys are read from the environment first and from these files as a
# fallback. They are matched by name rather than by extension because a `.txt`
# allowlist elsewhere would otherwise re-admit them — the same default-deny
# reasoning the data/ block uses.
.env
secrets/
openrouterapi.txt
*api*key*.txt
*_api.txt

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv*/
.tox/
.nox/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.hypothesis/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# QuickUMLS index — derived from licensed UMLS content, never committed
**/quickumls_index/
*.unqlite

# Downloaded experiment results: derived from MIMIC-IV under the PhysioNet DUA,
# and 200 MB+ per run. The bucket is the system of record; a local copy is a
# working convenience, not something to version.
results/

# Experiment run directories. `run1/` held a 163 MB SQLite prediction store whose
# `document_id` column is real MIMIC `hadm_id`s — derived restricted data under the
# PhysioNet DUA, and it sat here untracked but unignored. `runs/` above covers the
# corruption engine's own output; this covers the downstream harness's, which names
# its directories by run id.
run[0-9]*/

# Prediction stores and any other embedded database. Matched by extension as well as
# by directory because a run directory can be renamed and the SQLite file inside it is
# still a SQLite file — the same default-deny reasoning the data/ block uses.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# `sample_output/` is deliberately NOT ignored. Every value in it is fabricated
# (`run_summary.json` opens by saying so) and `tests/test_mipa_metrics.py` reads
# it as a fixture. It is the one results-shaped directory that is safe to commit,
# which is exactly why it is named here rather than left to a general rule.

# The manuscript: prose, figures, tables for the paper, the appendix workbook
# and the measured results they quote. Kept local on purpose. This repository
# holds the pipeline that corrupts the notes and scores the model; what the
# paper says about the results is written, checked and versioned elsewhere, and
# pre-publication text and numbers should not acquire a public history.
manuscript/

# Planning notes, drafts of requirements and superseded one-off scripts.
internal/
